":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Conceptual examples (not regulatory text)**\n\n- **MF class burdening ETF class:** MF cash purchases and redemptions force portfolio trading; commissions, spreads and market impact fall on all holders, including ETF holders. Redemption-driven sales can realize gains distributed to both classes.\n- **ETF class burdening MF class:** Cash creations or custom baskets can shift trading costs or portfolio drift onto MF holders. Conversely, ETF in-kind redemptions shed low-basis lots, a tax benefit shared unevenly.\n\n**Monitoring categories**\n\n- **Transaction costs:** which class's flows cause trading, and whether fees offset them.\n- **Cash:** MF redemption buffers creating cash drag for ETF holders.\n- **Gains:** realizations and distributions attributable to each class.\n\n**Representative order-specific framework (as of 2026-11-06)**\n\nUnder share-class exemptive orders, the board approves policies addressing cross-subsidization and receives periodic adviser reporting. Metrics, frequency and escalation triggers are fund-specific; no universal thresholds apply.","ttft_ms":6835,"type":"result","duration_ms":9213,"uuid":"0f259a44-be9d-4ae8-b6fc-6e01440ee064","ttft_stream_ms":1177,"time_to_request_ms":71,"first_content_frame_ms":1178,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
